==================================================================
#16: c-m degeneracy -- does the fuzzy-DM mass keep c natural?
==================================================================

  degeneracy line:  c(m) = 0.974 * (m / 2e-20 eV)^(1/4)

  landmark                          m (eV)    -> c   naturalness
  ----------------------------------------------------------
  model pin (amp+abundance)        2.0e-20    0.97   comfortable
  Lyman-alpha lower bound          2.0e-20    0.97   comfortable
  UFD Dalal-Kravtsov bound         3.0e-19    1.92   edge of O(1)
  if pushed to CDM-like            1.0e-18    2.59   strained

  c reaches 2 at  m = 3.6e-19 eV

  c reaches 3 at  m = 1.8e-18 eV

  c reaches 4 at  m = 5.7e-18 eV

------------------------------------------------------------------
VERDICT ON THE UFD TENSION:
  If UFD wins (m~3e-19), the model ABSORBS it by setting c = 1.92.
  That is still O(1) and 'natural' -- so the UFD tension is SURVIVABLE, NOT a kill.
  Cost: it spends c's naturalness margin (0.97 -> 1.9, toward the edge).
  And c is pinned only as tightly as m is measured: m in [2e-20, 3e-19]
  => c in [0.97, 1.92]. A RANGE, consistent w/ natural,
  not yet a sharp value. #16 gives c to a factor ~2, bounded by the mass data.
==================================================================
